<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,293.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,293.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,293 today from 1,287 on Aug 14, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1344    12.200	  1351    12.263</p>
<p>   1a   1251  9471.000	  1252  9481.000</p>
<p>   2    1577    22.536	  1576    22.519</p>
<p>   2a   1505 12343.000	  1501 12306.000</p>
<p>   3    1404    12.950	  1393    12.850</p>
<p>   3a   1212  9564.000	  1185  9356.000</p>
<p>   6    1297    13.379	  1293    13.331</p>
<p>   7    1190     5.793	  1185     5.769</p>
<p>   8     846     9.300	   844     9.281</p>
<p>   9     716  6257.000	   708  6188.000</p>
<p>  10    1152     5.821	  1148     5.800</p>
